---
title: Crispy Sheet-Pan Noodles with Glazed Tofu
description: Instant ramen baked on a sheet pan until crisp, with hoisin-maple glazed tofu and baby bok choy.
tags: [noodles, sheet-pan]
course: main
icons: [bowl-chopsticks-noodles, leafy-green, oven]
source:
  name: NYT Cooking
  author: Hetty Lui McKinnon
  url: https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1022637-crispy-sheet-pan-noodles-with-glazed-tofu
servings: 4
time: 35m
---

Heat the oven to 450°F (230°C) and place one rack on the top and one on the bottom.

Fill a #kettle{} or medium pot with water (about 8 cups) and bring to a boil. Place the @instant ramen noodles{3%blocks}(about 9 oz, flavor packets discarded) in a heatproof #bowl{} and cover with boiling water. Soak for ~soak{5%minutes}, then drain. Set aside the bowl to use for the bok choy.

Whisk the marinade in a #medium bowl{}: the @hoisin sauce{2%tbsp}, @sesame oil{1%tbsp}, @maple syrup{1%tbsp}, @garlic clove{1}(grated) and @sesame seeds{1%tsp}.

Place the noodles on a #sheet pan{}. Add the @&sesame oil{2%tbsp}, @neutral oil{1%tbsp}(such as grapeseed or vegetable), @soy sauce{2%tbsp} and @kosher salt{1/2%tsp}(such as Diamond Crystal). Toss to combine, then evenly spread out the noodles.

Dip each slice of @extra-firm tofu{1%package}(14 oz, patted dry and cut into 1/4-inch-thick slices) into the marinade, coating both sides, then add them to the sheet pan, pushing the noodles aside so that the tofu touches the pan and doesn't just sit on top of the noodles. Place on the bottom rack of the oven and bake for ~bake{15%minutes}. Reserve the excess marinade.

Place the @baby bok choy{3}(trimmed and sliced vertically into 4 pieces) into the reserved bowl, then add the remaining @&neutral oil{1%tbsp} and @&kosher salt{1/2%tsp}, and toss to coat.

Remove the sheet pan from the oven (the noodles should be crisp on the bottom and at the edges) and add the bok choy to the pan. Return the sheet pan to the top rack of the oven and bake for ~bake{4-7%minutes} until the greens are vibrant with crispy edges, and the tops of the noodles are crispy.

Drizzle with the remaining marinade, top with the @fresh cilantro{1%handful}(leaves) and serve.
